# `distinct *` takes no other columns (M1-19).
mode: syntax
---- query
from T | distinct *, a
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..23
  PIPELINE@0..22
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    NAME_REF@5..6
      IDENT@5..6 "T"
    WHITESPACE@6..7 " "
    PIPE@7..8 "|"
    WHITESPACE@8..9 " "
    DISTINCT_OP@9..22
      IDENT@9..17 "distinct"
      WHITESPACE@17..18 " "
      STAR@18..19 "*"
      COMMA@19..20 ","
      WHITESPACE@20..21 " "
      NAME_REF@21..22
        IDENT@21..22 "a"
  WHITESPACE@22..23 "\n"

error[DS0116]: `distinct *` cannot list other columns
  --> query:1:19
  |
1 | from T | distinct *, a
  |                   ^ `*` already means every column
  |
  = help: remove `*` to keep the distinct values of the listed columns, or remove the columns to keep distinct rows
